First 100 = open, which is Home Assistant spec.
Home Assistant has a range for open/close from 0, 100, which are the second and third parameters.

The reverse parameter means the scale in Tuya is reversed (so in most cases, this will send a 0 to Tuya).

This matches the behavior of the current_position:

```py
    @property
    def current_cover_position(self) -> int | None:
        """Return cover current position."""
        if self._current_position_type is None:
            return None

        if not self._position_dpcode:
            return None

        if (position := self.device.status.get(self._position_dpcode)) is None:
            return None

        return round(
            self._current_position_type.remap_value_to(position, 0, 100, reverse=True)
        )
```

This also flips the scale when retrieving the position from Tuya, hence we should flip it when sending/change it as well. The same logic can be observed in the `set_position` method.
